200 with the fixed first mass of 110 m/z. The AGC target for the MS2 was 1e5, and the maximum injection time was 60 ms. Precursors were fragmented by higher-energy collision dissociation (HCD) with the normalized collision energy of 28. Only precursors with charge states 3-7 with an intensity higher than 1000 were selected for fragmentation, and the dynamic exclusion was set to 45 s. Each sample was analyzed in three times. For fractionated cross-linked peptides, the separation gradient was achieved by applying 2-7% B for 10s, 7-23% B for 50 min, 23-40% B for 20 min, 40-80% B for 2 min, and 80% B for 13 min. The AGC target for the MS2 was 5e4 and the dynamic exclusion was set to 18 s. The other parameter settings are the same as above. Each fractionation was analyzed in three times.\n'}], 'model': 'gpt-5.4-nano-2026-03-17', 'store': True, 'temperature': 0.3}}
